"""Reviewed remaining fixed Hoenn actor conversation endings; voice order is canonical."""
ROWS = []
def add(key, labels, subject, lines):
    replies = [line.strip() for line in lines.split('|')]
    assert len(replies) == 11, (key, len(replies))
    ROWS.append(dict(key='hoenn_final_' + key, labels=labels.split(), subject=subject, replies=replies))

add('blender_record','BerryBlender_Text_SetNewBlenderRecord','A blender participant aims to set a speed record today.','''laughing~The berries have been warned. Today they become very fast jam.|An ambitious experiment. Keeping the timing consistent should help more than frightening the machine.|Set your record. Keep all fingers outside it.|That is a lot of confidence for something with a lid.|Fast is good, but a smooth batch still gets my vote.|A speed record, with fruit as the unwilling witnesses.|The berries have accepted that their remaining time is brief.|Now that is a machine worth watching for wobble.|A small whirlpool with a very personal deadline.|Set the record without wearing the ingredients, please.|We should watch the first batch. That is quite a claim.''')
add('blender_cute','BerryBlender_Text_MakeDeliciousPokeblocks','A participant plans delicious Pokeblocks to make their Pokemon cuter.','''soft_smile~A snack that makes you cuter? I may need a very small serving.|Taste and condition in the same experiment. A rather pleasant research subject.|Good food and a happy partner. Sensible plan.|They already sound fond of their Pokemon. That helps.|Delicious comes first. A treat should actually be a treat.|The road to glory apparently passes through the snack bowl.|A little block of sugar and very large expectations.|Tiny food cubes with carefully specified cuteness requirements.|I like that delicious made it into the plan.|Presentation matters, but I respect a recipe that remembers flavor.|Their Pokemon is getting the enthusiastic chef treatment today.''')
add('blender_invite','BerryBlender_Text_LookGoodAtBlendingJoinUs','A blender participant invites the player to join the group.','''soft_smile~We look good at blending? My sleeves have fooled another expert.|A friendly invitation. We have not even submitted a sample batch.|They have room at the blender. Worth a look.|That was kind. We do look less nervous from a distance.|More hands make a smoother batch, if everyone keeps the beat.|Recruited on appearance alone. Our stirring reputation precedes us.|We have somehow acquired the face of a competent blender.|A group project with edible results sounds promising.|A place at the table offered before we earned it. Lovely.|Apparently we have the look of people who can handle berries.|They spotted us and made space. That is a nice welcome.''')
add('island_family','DewfordTown_House1_Text_LotToBeSaidForLivingOnIsland','A resident values island life with family and Pokemon.','''soft_smile~Family, Pokemon, and the sea. That is a pretty good little island inventory.|A small community can hold a rather complete life.|Sounds like they have what matters close by.|They sound comfortable here. I like that.|A table with family and Pokemon nearby sounds full enough.|A whole good life, requiring remarkably little mainland.|The island is small. Their affection for it is not.|Everything important is within walking distance. Efficient and lovely.|Some people put down roots where others see only water.|They make island living sound very well chosen.|That is a home described by who shares it.''')
add('island_marriage','DewfordTown_House1_Text_LifeGoesSlowlyOnIsland','A woman who moved from Slateport finds happiness in Dewfords sea and slower life.','''soft_smile~She traded a big port for a little island and likes the change. Good trade.|She knows both places. That makes her contentment quite convincing.|Slower suits her. Glad the move worked out.|The sea sounds like part of what made this home.|A quiet meal tastes different when nobody has to rush off.|A marriage, a crossing, and a life she is happy to call hers.|She escaped the hurry without having to escape the sea.|Less traffic, more ocean. A compelling redesign of the day.|The water stayed, and the pace changed. She found her place.|She chose a smaller town without making her life smaller.|I like hearing what she gained from leaving the port.''')
add('brawly_fan','DewfordTown_House2_Text_BrawlySoCool','A boy admires Brawly and assumes visitors may share his enthusiasm.','''laughing~We crossed the sea and landed right in Brawly's fan club.|Brawly appears to have excellent local approval ratings.|That is one proud hometown fan.|He almost sounds surprised there are other reasons to visit.|A town should be allowed to brag about someone it loves.|Our voyage has been assigned a celebrity destination.|He has already written Brawly onto our itinerary.|That is impressive enthusiasm for one Gym Leader.|Admiration travels quickly on a little island.|Brawly has a very dedicated unofficial publicity office.|You can tell who the local favorite is before reaching the Gym.''')
add('fainted_hm','DewfordTown_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_FaintedMonCanUseHM','A resident explains that fainted Pokemon can still use HM field moves.','''surprised~They can still help outside battle? Even so, I vote for getting them a rest.|Field ability and battle readiness are distinct. Healing remains a good next step.|Useful to know. We still get them healed.|I would rather give them a quiet break first.|That may help us get home, where they can rest properly.|A surprising reserve of competence after the battle is over.|Still helpful while exhausted. An uncomfortably familiar talent.|Good to know the field move is available in a pinch.|They can help us reach safety. Then we can help them recover.|Capability does not make a tired partner any less tired.|A useful distinction, especially if the Center is across some water.''')
add('cavern_stones','DewfordTown_PokemonCenter_1F_Text_StoneCavern','A resident has heard that the nearby stone cavern contains rare stones.','''soft_smile~A stone cavern with rare stones. Finally, a place with an honest name.|A rumor worth checking, provided we bring enough light.|We can look. Watch the footing in there.|I like a treasure hunt that does not demand an audience.|Water and a packed lunch first. Stones are heavy souvenirs.|The cavern is advertising a premium selection of itself.|Rare stones, ordinary darkness. Bring a light.|Interesting minerals nearby? My pockets are already underqualified.|The island keeps some of its curiosities underground.|A rare stone could make a lovely find, mud permitting.|We have a local lead now, rather than just a dark entrance.''')

add('beauty_happiness','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_WinBeautyContestMakesMeHappy','A spectator admits that winning Beauty Contests brings extra happiness.','''soft_smile~Winning makes them extra happy. A ribbon with a bonus serving of happy.|They seem to have isolated their favorite kind of victory.|Good. Enjoy the wins you worked for.|It is nice when someone simply admits they enjoy this.|A little extra joy is a good reason to enter.|A perfectly honest review: winning is rather pleasant.|They found a reliable source of unusually good days.|An outcome measured in happiness. I approve of that metric.|Some ribbons mean more to the person holding them.|Beauty wins suit their mood very well, apparently.|That little admission says a lot about their favorite contest.''')
add('beauty_glitz','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_GanderAtAllThosePrettyPokemon','An audience member delights in the contests beautiful Pokemon and glitz.','''laughing~The sparkle has reached maximum sparkle. That laugh is the proof.|An enthusiastic observer. The display has clearly achieved its purpose.|They are having a good time. Let them enjoy it.|Their laugh carries farther than the applause.|That is the sound of someone getting exactly what they came for.|An audience member gloriously immune to restrained appreciation.|A cheerful avalanche of glitz has claimed another victim.|All that shine and a very satisfied spectator.|There is room for loud joy among all this careful beauty.|Now that is someone who appreciates a little spectacle.|I could pick out their laugh from across the whole hall.''')
add('beauty_grooming','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_CantWinOnBeautyAlone','A contestant says careful grooming matters alongside natural beauty.','''soft_smile~Apparently the shine needs maintenance. Even a champion can have bed fur.|Condition does take work. Natural appearance is only one variable.|Looking after your partner shows. Keep it gentle.|All that gloss probably took more time than we see.|Daily care tends to show up when the big day arrives.|Behind every effortless shine, apparently, is a busy brush.|Beauty has a maintenance schedule. How inconveniently honest.|The finish matters, and so does the work beneath it.|Care leaves a visible mark, even on a glossy coat.|They have a point. Good grooming is part of presentation.|We see the shine now, but someone put the hours in.''')
add('beauty_distracted_judge','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_EveryPokemonPristineBeauty','A judge is so impressed by the Pokemon that they nearly forget to score.','''laughing~The judge got dazzled out of judging. Somebody hand them a pencil.|Admiration is appropriate. Recording the scores is also advisable.|Enjoy the show. Remember the numbers.|That is a flattering problem for the contestants to cause.|A wonderful dish still needs its judge to finish tasting.|The critic has been defeated by the very subject of criticism.|Beauty has temporarily disabled the arithmetic.|A clipboard might need a little reminder bell.|Even the person measuring beauty can forget the measure.|An excellent compliment, though I would still like a fair score.|Those must be some very distracting performances.''')
add('beauty_mc','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_AreYouEnteringBeautyContest','The Beauty Contest MC wishes a prospective entrant good luck.','''soft_smile~Good luck delivered right to us. Very convenient contest service.|A pleasant welcome from the person organizing the event.|Friendly welcome. Now we know where to start.|That makes entering sound a little less intimidating.|A kind word before a contest can settle the nerves.|The master of ceremonies has supplied our opening encouragement.|An official blessing with pleasantly little paperwork.|Enthusiastic staff make a complicated event feel approachable.|A little luck offered freely is always welcome.|A warm welcome looks good on the whole event.|The MC found a moment to encourage us. Nice.''')
add('beauty_confidence','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_EyesWillBeGluedToMyBeauty','A confident contestant expects every eye to stay on their beautiful Pokemon.','''smug~That is a lot of confidence. The Pokemon may need its own sunglasses.|A strong prediction. The other entrants may complicate it.|Confident partner. We will see how it goes.|They already seem to be enjoying the attention.|Confidence is useful, as long as the Pokemon enjoys this too.|Every eye, they say. A modest request from our local phenomenon.|The audience has apparently lost the right to blink.|They have certainly optimized the announcement of their own entry.|Such certainty could fill the hall before the performance does.|They know their best feature and have announced it thoroughly.|Now I am curious whether the performance matches that confidence.''')
add('overgroomed','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_OverdidGrooming','A contestant is distressed after excessive grooming leaves their Pokemon scraggly.','''sad~Oh, poor little scraggle. Put the brush down and give that coat a break.|More brushing will likely worsen this. A gentle rest is the sensible next step.|Stop brushing. Check that the skin is all right.|They meant well. I feel bad for both of them.|A soft cloth and a break sound better than another rescue brushing.|An overzealous brush has written a rather unfortunate twist.|The pursuit of perfection has left a tiny, scruffy witness.|Time to stop adjusting the thing that needs to recover.|Let the coat rest. Not every tangle needs an immediate answer.|A small grooming disaster calls for restraint now, darling.|Their panic is understandable. I would check on the Pokemon first.''')
add('aurora_visibility','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_JudgeWontSeeAuroraBeam','A contestant realizes an Aurora Beam too dazzling to see would be pointless.','''laughing~An invisible victory is going to be difficult to show the judge.|An excellent correction. Visibility is rather central to a visual appeal.|Good catch. Let the judge actually see it.|I like that they caught the flaw themselves.|Too much of a good thing can spoil the whole serving.|A dazzling master plan, briefly undone by the need for witnesses.|The beam has achieved the fatal flaw of being too impressive.|Brightness controls would solve an unusually literal presentation problem.|Light needs a little darkness around it to be seen.|Dazzle the audience while leaving them an audience, please.|That realization arrived just in time to save everyone's eyes.''')
add('younger_me','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_PokemonLooksLikeYoungerMe','A woman wonders why her husband spat coffee at her youthful Pokemon comparison.','''laughing~Maybe the coffee was surprised too. I would ask him after he stops coughing.|The timing suggests the comparison surprised him. His explanation remains untested.|Ask him. Preferably after he puts the cup down.|I would not want to be holding that second cup.|Whatever he meant, the table probably needs a cloth now.|Her husband has issued a highly ambiguous review in coffee.|A dangerous moment to discover that your spouse has opinions.|That is why liquid and sudden commentary need separate workspaces.|Some answers arrive as a spray before becoming words.|He owes her an explanation and the table an apology.|That reaction raised more questions than the comparison did.''')
add('two_categories','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_TodayWonSmartnessContest','A boy boasts that his former Beauty winner has now won Smartness too.','''laughing~Pretty AND clever! The ribbon shelf may need a second floor.|Success in two categories suggests thoughtful preparation.|Two kinds of win. Give the Pokemon some credit too.|They sound delighted enough for both victories.|That partner has earned an excellent celebratory snack.|A double triumph, followed by a remarkably fearless self-review.|Beauty and brains. The rest of us may return quietly to our seats.|Versatility confirmed. That is a very capable little contender.|A familiar partner can still reveal another strength.|A second category win is quite the addition to the portfolio.|I would love to hear how differently they prepared for each one.''')
add('contest_categories','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_EnteredBunchOfContests','An experienced entrant describes how move categories affect Coolness appeals.','''soft_smile~So a clever move can be the wrong kind of clever. Contests are picky.|The category changes how an appeal is received. Experience is useful here.|Know the event before choosing the moves.|A good performance still needs the right room.|Like choosing a flavor for the right dish. Context matters.|The same act, reviewed by a very different set of expectations.|Even cleverness can apparently arrive underdressed for the category.|Matching the move to the scoring system saves a lot of guesswork.|Every gathering has its own idea of a pleasing gesture.|Read the category before styling the whole performance.|Repeated entries taught them something a single win might not.''')
add('want_cute_partner','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_WantCuteMonOfMyOwn','A spectator is inspired by cute contestants to catch a Pokemon.','''soft_smile~The cuteness worked. Someone is about to make a new little friend.|A lively demonstration of how enthusiasm spreads.|Good luck finding a partner who suits you.|Seeing them together does make companionship look lovely.|Bring patience along. Cute friends still have strong opinions.|The contest has acquired an unexpected recruitment function.|A dangerous hall for anyone trying to resist adorable company.|One look at the entrants and the plans for the day changed.|May the new friendship be even better than the first impression.|Cuteness has made its case with devastating efficiency.|That is a sweet reason to begin looking for a partner.''')
add('wrong_cute_subject','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_ThatGirlThereIsCutest','A spectator has been judging a girl instead of the Pokemon.','''laughing~Wrong contestants! The Pokemon would like their attention back.|A fundamental error in identifying the subjects of the contest.|Eyes on the Pokemon. They did the preparation.|That is an awkward thing to realize out loud.|The little contestants deserve their turn in the spotlight.|Our amateur judge has mistaken the entire cast.|An impressive failure to understand the assignment.|First step in scoring: correctly identify what is being scored.|They watched the same hall and saw quite another event.|A category error with an unfortunately public explanation.|I wonder how long they had been confidently watching the wrong thing.''')
add('water_sport_cute','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_SuchCharmingCuteAppeals','The Cute judge delights in an adorable Water Sport appeal.','''soft_smile~Even a little splash can steal the show. That judge is thoroughly splashed.|Water Sport has evidently been presented to excellent effect.|That appeal found exactly the right audience.|It must have been lovely to get that reaction.|A simple move can shine when the partner enjoys it.|A modest splash has received a magnificent review.|The judge has discovered a new reason to adore water.|That is a very successful use of a surprisingly simple move.|A little water, a little charm, and a delighted witness.|An adorable splash is a surprisingly complete aesthetic.|The judge's face probably said as much as the score.''')
add('contest_mc_busy','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_InTheMiddleOfContest','The MC redirects a visitor to registration during an ongoing contest.','''flustered~Right! Counter first, dramatic entrance later. We got those backwards.|Registration keeps the running event orderly. We should follow that route.|Counter first. Give them room to work.|Oh. We probably wandered in at a bad moment.|Let them finish serving this group before we join the next.|Our surprise entrance has received a polite logistical correction.|We have been gently removed from the list of scheduled surprises.|The event has an entry point. We accidentally found the middle.|A little patience will get us through the proper door.|A gracious redirection after our rather premature arrival.|We should let the current contestants keep everyone's attention.''')
add('azurill_distracted','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_MyAzurillWasDistracted','A trainer worries that their Azurill was distracted by another Pokemon.','''soft_smile~Azurill found an extra contestant interesting. Tiny audience of one.|A crowded hall has plenty of distractions for a small Pokemon.|It happens. Help Azurill settle before the next appeal.|Poor little thing. There is a lot to notice in here.|A familiar voice might help more than getting upset.|An unscheduled supporting character has stolen Azurill's attention.|Azurill briefly reviewed a different performance.|Too many exciting inputs for one tiny contestant.|A gentle call may bring that wandering attention home.|The hall has plenty of competition for a little one's attention.|I wonder which Pokemon caught Azurill's eye.''')
add('contest_strength','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_NeverWonBattleButContest','A trainer says their Pokemon excels at contests despite never winning battles.','''soft_smile~Found the right kind of winning! That partner had a talent waiting.|Different activities reveal different abilities. A lovely example.|They found what suits their partner. Good.|It must feel wonderful to see that confidence bloom.|Everyone deserves a place where their best qualities show.|An overlooked contender has found the perfect kind of triumph.|A different arena, and suddenly the world has better manners.|The Pokemon worked fine. The task needed changing.|Some gifts become visible only when we look another way.|A partner with a very specific talent deserves a fitting venue.|That is a story worth hearing from the trainer who noticed.''')
add('petal_dance','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_PetalDanceIsMarvel','A trainer praises their Pokemons elegant Petal Dance and guards its performance.','''soft_smile~An elegant dance with its own very determined security guard.|We can appreciate the move without interrupting its execution.|Give them room. They are concentrating.|I would like to watch quietly from here.|Then we should let the Pokemon finish its lovely moment.|A marvel of elegance, protected by an admirably firm announcement.|The petals may be delicate. The boundary is perfectly clear.|Enough clear floor space makes a performance much easier.|Some things are best welcomed with a little silence.|A beautiful presentation deserves room to breathe.|Their pride is obvious. We can watch without getting in the way.''')
add('cuter_claim','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_MyMonAppealSoMuchCuter','A contestant praises others then predicts their own Pokemon will be much cuter.','''smug~A compliment with a little competitive elbow tucked inside it.|A favorable hypothesis about their own entry. Evidence to follow.|Nice confidence. Let the appeal do the talking.|They almost made it through the compliment without competing.|They can appreciate the others and still back their partner.|An elegant compliment that quietly turns into a declaration of war.|They admire the competition from a very comfortable imagined podium.|We have a claim. Next comes the demonstration.|Affection does make our own companions look a little brighter.|Very sweet opening. Very sharp little finish.|I would like to compare that prediction with the actual audience reaction.''')
add('pokeblock_question','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_ManWhoWonEarlierHadPokeblocks','A girl wonders whether a previous winners many Pokeblocks explain his success.','''soft_smile~A bag full of snacks is a strong opening argument. Not quite a trophy yet.|Quantity alone tells us little about the quality or preparation.|They might help. The Pokemon still has to perform.|It is easy to notice the snacks and miss all the practice.|Good Pokeblocks help condition, but a full bag is no guarantee.|A winning secret glimpsed through the contents of somebody's pockets.|If carrying treats guaranteed victory, many pockets would be famous.|We need more information than the number of cubes in his bag.|What he shared with his partner matters more than what he carried.|Preparation can be visible without telling the whole story.|That is a useful question to ask the winner himself.''')
add('huge_contest','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_IsntThisPlaceHumongous','A sailor contrasts Lilycoves huge tense contest hall with smaller halls.','''surprised~This place has enough room for everyone's nerves to echo.|The larger venue certainly changes how the atmosphere feels.|Big hall. Same need to keep your head.|I can see why a smaller hall might feel easier.|A crowd this size makes even familiar work feel different.|The grand venue has supplied a grander variety of nerves.|The tension has acquired excellent acoustics.|That is a lot of space to fill with one little performance.|A large room can make a heartbeat feel rather loud.|The scale certainly changes the impression at the door.|They noticed the atmosphere before any appeal even began.''')
add('grandpa_cheer','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_YoureBeautifulGrandpa','A spectator enthusiastically cheers Grandpa as beautiful.','''laughing~Grandpa has a fan club, and its volume is excellent.|A very supportive audience member. Impossible to mistake their allegiance.|Grandpa has backup. Loud backup.|That cheer is sweet. Also very hard to miss.|Someone came ready to celebrate their family.|Grandpa's acclaim has arrived several rows ahead of him.|A beautiful grandpa and a wonderfully unrestrained supporter.|Enthusiasm successfully transmitted across the entire hall.|May he hear every bit of that proud little shout.|Grandpa is receiving the full star treatment.|I would love to see his face when he hears that.''')
add('different_appeals','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_AllSeemToUseDifferentMoves','An audience member notices individual move styles even among identical species.','''soft_smile~Same Pokemon, different surprises. Like hats, but with more explosions.|Species does not determine a trainer's entire choice of approach.|Same kind of partner. Different ways to work together.|It makes each performance worth paying attention to.|Even the same ingredients can become very different dishes.|A familiar cast can still tell an entirely different story.|Sameness becomes much less convincing once they start moving.|There is plenty of room to invent within the same starting design.|The differences appear when we let them show us.|Style is in the choices, even with a familiar silhouette.|That is the sort of detail you catch by really watching.''')
add('smarter_than_trainers','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_PokemonSmarterThanTrainers','A spectator thinks the Pokemon seem much smarter than their trainers.','''laughing~I will politely avoid asking which half of our team looks smarter.|An interesting assessment, though the trainers may dispute the sample.|Partners cover each other's weak spots. Often quietly.|I am going to let the Pokemon take that compliment.|Sometimes the one being looked after knows exactly what to do.|A devastating review delivered to the wrong end of the partnership.|At last, someone is willing to say what the Pokemon suspected.|The operator is occasionally the least reliable component.|Wisdom does not always stand on two feet.|The contestants received a compliment with considerable collateral damage.|Now I am watching the trainers' reactions as well.''')
add('smart_green','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_StillLoveSmartnessContests','A fan loves Smartness Contests and their intellectual green color.','''soft_smile~Green makes them feel clever. I should apologize to several shrubs.|Their preference combines the category and its color quite neatly.|They know what they like. Green included.|That is a very specific, rather endearing favorite.|A favorite color can make an already good event feel better.|Intellectual green: a shade with an impressive education.|The color has apparently completed its studies.|I had not considered assigning intellectual credentials to paint.|Some colors seem to hold exactly the thought we like.|An intellectual green is a wonderfully confident color description.|Now I am curious what the other contest colors suggest to them.''')
add('four_friends_contest','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_AreYouEnjoyingThisContest','The Smartness judge encourages entering a contest with three friends.','''soft_smile~Three friends and a contest. That is a very sparkly group outing.|A shared entry could make comparing approaches particularly interesting.|Bring friends. Keep the rivalry friendly.|That sounds less daunting than entering alone.|A little friendly competition makes a good outing together.|Four friends arrive; one evening acquires several competing narrators.|An invitation to discover how gracious your friends are about losing.|Four approaches to the same challenge would be fun to compare.|Company can turn a nervous entrance into a pleasant adventure.|Friends make excellent company, even across a score sheet.|I like that the judge invited us to share the experience.''')
add('smart_mc','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_GiveItBestSmartAppeal','The MC rallies entrants to show their best Smartness appeals.','''laughing~Brains ready! Mine are making a slightly nervous rattling noise.|A clear invitation to demonstrate preparation. No pressure from me.|Ready enough. Let the partner focus.|That announcement makes the moment feel very real.|Time to trust the care and practice already put in.|The challenge has been issued. Intelligence is requested immediately.|Our thoughts have been formally summoned to appear in public.|Good moment to stop adjusting and begin the actual demonstration.|Let the clever work speak when the room grows quiet.|A confident opening announcement can do wonders for the atmosphere.|Everyone's attention just shifted toward the next appeal.''')
add('wrong_smart_contest','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_EnteredWrongContest','A trainer entered a tough Pokemon in Smartness and hopes Rock Smash will look clever.','''laughing~A smart-looking Rock Smash? Maybe it can smash something educational.|A difficult mismatch, though presentation may still make an impression.|Wrong contest. Make the best of the entry.|I feel for them. That is a hard mistake to realize here.|They can still support their partner through an awkward round.|A clerical error has become a bold artistic experiment.|When in doubt, break a rock with scholarly intent.|We have an unexpected design constraint and one very strong solution.|The rock may learn something from the encounter.|Confidence will have to do some rather heavy styling work.|I am now extremely curious how they make this look smart.''')
add('wise_partner','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_RaisedMonToBeSmart','An older contestant proudly presents a Pokemon raised with years of wisdom to their wife.','''soft_smile~Years of cleverness, and someone special watching. That is a big little moment.|Long preparation deserves recognition. I hope his wife enjoys seeing the result.|A lot of work brought them here. Respect that.|The way he asks his wife to watch is lovely.|That is years of care arriving together at one contest.|A lifetime of preparation, with one particularly important audience member.|All that wisdom, and he still wants his wife to see.|A carefully developed partnership with a very proud demonstration.|The years are present in his voice, and so is affection.|His partner has experience and an enthusiastically loyal household.|I would watch for his wife's reaction when the appeal begins.''')
add('next_smart_move','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_IfMonPullsSmartMoveNext','A contestant anticipates that a smart next move will bring audience excitement to its peak.','''surprised~They can feel the big moment coming. Do not sneeze now, anyone.|The audience response seems close to the threshold they want.|They have an opening. Stay focused.|That is the breath before everyone starts cheering.|Timing can make the next little touch count for so much.|A whole room balanced on the promise of the next move.|Anticipation has everyone politely holding their lungs.|One well chosen input could push the response right to the top.|The room is waiting. Their partner only needs its moment.|They have read the audience well. Now comes the finish.|You can almost see them following the crowd's attention.''')
add('leech_life_cute','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_DontAppreciateCuteLeechLife','A trainer repeatedly used Zubats Leech Life and resents the audience disliking it.','''flustered~Zubat may be darling, but the audience has had its recommended daily biting.|Affection may be influencing their assessment of repetition.|They love Zubat. The crowd still gets an opinion.|A favorite move can lose its surprise after a few turns.|Even a favorite dish benefits from a little variety.|A devoted admirer confronts the scandal of other people's taste.|Their darling has drained the audience's enthusiasm rather efficiently.|Repeating the same appeal probably needs a different feedback loop.|Love sees charm where strangers may only see teeth.|Darling Zubat might need a second trick for this particular crowd.|I admire the loyalty. I can also understand the audience tiring of it.''')

add('contest_artist','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_ContestFeastForEyes','An artist finds the contest Pokemon inspiring subjects to paint.','''soft_smile~So many beautiful models, and none promised to sit still.|A lively subject collection. Capturing movement would be the challenge.|Plenty to paint. Ask before crowding their partners.|They sound almost overwhelmed with ideas. I know that feeling.|A feast for the eyes sounds like a very satisfying afternoon.|An artist has found enough inspiration to exhaust several canvases.|All these willing muses, provided they are willing to hold still.|I would need an enormous sketchbook just to start.|A good sight can ask quietly to become something else.|The colors and poses would make a magnificent study.|I like watching what catches an artist's eye in a crowd.''')
add('master_cute','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_MasterRankHereICome','A Black Belt excitedly declares their Pokemon the cutest before Master Rank.','''laughing~That is a very fierce declaration of cuteness. I believe the cuteness is armed.|Strong affection and strong confidence. Quite a combination.|They back their partner completely. Good start.|The little laugh at the end makes this rather sweet.|That much pride probably came from a lot of care.|The world has been summoned to recognize one extremely adorable champion.|Master Rank approaches. Cuteness is taking no prisoners.|A very powerful delivery system for a very tender opinion.|Their fierce certainty is protecting something rather gentle.|That is the most intimidating endorsement of cuteness I have heard.|Now I really want to see the partner inspiring that announcement.''')
add('blender_whoa','BerryBlender_Text_WhoaAwesome','A spectator responds with amazement to the Berry Blender.','''surprised~Yes! I do not know which bit impressed them most, but yes!|A concise and entirely positive observational report.|That got their attention. Fair enough.|It is nice to hear someone simply enjoy the moment.|A good batch can make people wonderfully eloquent.|A review so brief that enthusiasm occupies the entire sentence.|Words have briefly surrendered to astonishment.|That sounds like a successful demonstration to me.|Wonder does not always require a long explanation.|Sometimes the first delighted reaction is the best one.|I would look where they are looking right now.''')
add('blender_fast','BerryBlender_Text_WickedlyFast','A spectator marvels at the blenders speed.','''surprised~That fruit is going places, mostly in very small circles.|The rotation rate has clearly impressed the observers.|Fast enough to keep your hands well clear.|It is hard to follow the motion at that speed.|Those berries are getting the most energetic mixing of their lives.|A whirlwind with a remarkably specific culinary ambition.|The berries have no time left to reconsider.|I would love to know how well the bearings tolerate that.|A little storm, contained beneath a lid.|Quite a speed, provided the results stay off our clothes.|The whole group seems to be watching that spin.''')
add('blender_expert','BerryBlender_Text_WhatAnExpert','A bystander admires an expert blender operator.','''soft_smile~Expert berry whirling deserves expert applause. Mind the splash zone.|Practice becomes quite visible when the timing is this consistent.|They know what they are doing. Watch and learn.|It looks so easy when somebody has done it often.|That is the confidence of someone who knows their ingredients.|A master at work, with an unusually delicious field of expertise.|So this is what control over one's life looks like. It involves berries.|Smooth timing like that tells me they know the machine well.|Skill can be lovely even in the smallest everyday task.|Competence is always an excellent look.|I would ask how long it took them to get that good.''')
add('blender_impatient','BerryBlender_Text_LetsGetBlendingAlready','A blender participant is impatient to begin.','''laughing~The berries are ready, the person is ready, and patience has left.|The introductory phase has exceeded their preferred duration.|Ready to start. No mistaking that.|They have probably been waiting a while.|Ingredients ready? Then there is no need to let them wait.|Our eager collaborator would like to skip directly to the action.|Patience was apparently left outside with the coats.|I understand that urge to stop discussing a machine and use it.|Some people greet possibility by reaching for the handle.|Enthusiasm has a very short waiting list today.|Their whole attention is already on the next batch.''')
add('blender_result','BerryBlender_Text_WhatKindOfPokeblockWillIGet','A participant eagerly wonders what Pokeblock the batch will produce.','''soft_smile~A tiny mystery snack! I support this very edible suspense.|The ingredients and timing should make the result interesting.|We will find out when the batch is done.|That anticipation is half the fun of making something.|I always like the moment before tasting a new batch.|A thrilling mystery, with a conveniently bite-sized resolution.|For once, the unknown appears to have a pleasant flavor.|We have put in the ingredients. Now comes the reveal.|A little uncertainty can sweeten the wait.|I wonder what color the finished batch will be.|Their excitement is making me curious about the result too.''')
add('toughness_swoon','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_ToughContestIsExtreme','A fan swoons over muscular appeals and sweat in Toughness Contests.','''laughing~They came for the muscles and got the full splashy experience.|The physical presentation seems central to their enthusiasm.|They have a clear favorite. Very clear.|That is a lot of feeling about a very strenuous contest.|Someone should make sure the enthusiastic spectators have water too.|A passionate critic, overwhelmed by the sheer force of perspiration.|The atmosphere is apparently humid with admiration.|An event with impressive output and very enthusiastic cooling requirements.|Their delight has an oddly specific weather pattern.|They appreciate every strenuous detail of the presentation.|I would never have guessed sweat could get such a glowing review.''')
add('peaking_condition','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_LavishedCareOnMon','A trainer feels daily care has brought their Pokemon to peak contest condition.','''soft_smile~All that everyday care gets its big day today. Good luck to them.|Consistent preparation is a strong basis for confidence.|They put the work in. Time to trust their partner.|I like hearing pride in the quiet work before the contest.|Day after day of care matters more than one lucky morning.|The grand prediction rests on a great many ordinary, careful days.|Their certainty has been fed and groomed for quite some time.|That sounds like a well maintained partner ready for the real test.|The daily kindness is already something worth being proud of.|A polished result begins long before anyone sees the final look.|I would ask what part of their routine made the biggest difference.''')
add('daily_contest_stroll','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_WholeVarietyOfPokemonHere','A resident visits the contest hall daily to see many Pokemon.','''soft_smile~A daily stroll with a changing cast of little celebrities. Excellent route.|A regular visit offers a pleasantly varied set of observations.|Good place to see new partners without going far.|That sounds like a lovely reason to get out each day.|A little walk and a hall full of interesting company.|A daily audience member for a show that keeps changing.|A routine with enough variety to avoid feeling like one.|Same building, different Pokemon. Very efficient sightseeing.|Returning can still bring surprises when we look closely.|A daily dose of fresh faces and excellent presentation.|They probably notice changes that a one-time visitor would miss.''')
add('family_blending','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_MadePokeblocksWithFamily','A child proudly describes smooth Pokeblocks made with the whole family.','''soft_smile~The whole family helped! That batch has four sets of proud fingerprints.|Coordinated participation can improve the blend. A nice family experiment.|They worked together and made something good.|That sounds like the sort of afternoon a child remembers.|A good recipe and a family around it. Hard to improve on that.|A family production with an unusually smooth final act.|The snacks appear to have survived a committee beautifully.|Four people keeping time together is genuinely impressive.|The cubes hold a little bit of an afternoon together.|A family collaboration that turned out both smooth and memorable.|They are just as proud of who helped as of what they made.''')
add('motel_battles','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_GirlsAreCute','A visitor enthusiastically likes battles against Tubers and Twins.','''flustered~That is a very energetic list of favorite opponents. I hope the battles are fair.|They appear particularly enthusiastic about those trainer classes.|Enjoy the match. Respect the other trainer.|They certainly have a favorite kind of battle.|The young trainers deserve a fair challenge and a kind opponent.|A highly animated review of the local battle scene.|Their enthusiasm has more exclamation points than I can comfortably hold.|Double battles do give everyone a lot to keep track of.|Every opponent deserves to be treated with care.|A rather loud declaration of a very specific preference.|I would be more interested in hearing how the actual battles went.''')
add('gameboy_ready','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_NeverLeaveWithoutGameBoy','A visitor always carries a Game Boy Advance for unexpected challenges.','''laughing~Prepared for any challenge, provided it fits in that little machine.|A portable device does make spontaneous matches easier to arrange.|They travel prepared. Keep it out of the rain.|It is nice to have a familiar game ready wherever you go.|Something to share while waiting makes a useful travel companion.|Adventure is apparently incomplete without a smaller adventure in the pocket.|They have made boredom's survival considerably less likely.|Portable play is a very convincing engineering achievement.|A small familiar thing can make anywhere feel more welcoming.|One essential accessory, selected with admirable certainty.|I wonder how many friendships started with that little machine.''')
add('graphic_artist','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_ImTheGraphicArtist','A graphic artist asks whether Hoenns Pokemon are interesting.','''soft_smile~Very interesting! Some look as if their feet were a delightful last-minute idea.|The range of shapes and adaptations is certainly impressive.|Plenty of interesting partners around here.|There is always another little detail I had missed.|Their personalities make those interesting faces even better.|Hoenn offers an extraordinarily memorable collection of characters.|Some of them look like beautiful ideas that ignored all objections.|The variety of workable shapes is an endless source of curiosity.|An odd silhouette can become very dear once we know its owner.|Hoenn certainly has no shortage of striking designs.|I keep finding a new favorite detail in a familiar Pokemon.''')
add('programmer_slots','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_ImTheProgrammer','A programmer is surprised to be addressed and wonders about the local slots.','''soft_smile~We found the programmer during a very serious investigation of shiny levers.|An interesting local curiosity, though the outcomes may be costly data.|Just keep track of what you spend.|They seemed startled that we stopped to talk.|A little curiosity is fine. Keep enough money for the trip.|Our unexpected interview has interrupted a private study of the slots.|Even the programmer is susceptible to a suspiciously blinking machine.|I would be curious about the mechanisms before pulling anything.|Curiosity is a fine traveler, when it carries a little caution.|Those flashing lights do have a very deliberate appeal.|I wonder whether they watch the machine or the people playing it.''')
add('sea_breeze_heart','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_SeaBreezeTicklesHeart','A guest enjoys the sea breezes heartening sensation.','''soft_smile~The breeze found their heart. It mostly finds my loose hair.|A lovely description of a very immediate sensation.|Good air. Good place to pause a moment.|That is a gentle way to say it feels good here.|A sea breeze can make even a simple lunch feel special.|A tiny review of the coast, delivered entirely from the heart.|The wind is being unusually considerate today.|Fresh air does improve a room without any complicated machinery.|Some places reach us through the smallest moving things.|The coast has supplied its own excellent finishing touch.|They sound as though they have already found the best part of the visit.''')
add('partners_not_tools','LilycoveCity_House1_Text_PokemonPartnersNotTools','A resident insists Pokemon are partners and regrets that some people treat them as tools.','''sad~They have feelings and favorite places too. We should remember who is helping us.|Ability does not cancel a living partner's needs or preferences.|They trust us. We owe them better than being used.|I am glad someone said it so plainly.|Care belongs in the everyday things we do for our partners.|A partnership asks more of us than simply giving orders.|Being useful should never be the price of being treated kindly.|A partner gets a say. That changes how every plan should work.|A living being is more than what it can do for us.|Respect should be part of how a trainer carries themself.|You can learn a lot by watching how someone treats their Pokemon.''')
add('quadruplet_father','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_HappyToHaveQuadruplets','A father recalls his surprise at quadruplets and enjoys seeing them play together.','''soft_smile~Four little surprises, now playing together. His house must be wonderfully loud.|An unexpected family size, followed by a very genuine source of happiness.|Four at once. Glad he can enjoy the chaos.|Watching them together must make the busy days feel different.|That is a lot of small plates and a lot of love around the table.|The startling opening has become his favorite ongoing story.|Four simultaneous arrivals. I understand needing a moment to process that.|A household scaled up much faster than the original plan.|Surprise grew into a familiar, noisy kind of joy.|Four children means an impressive range of tiny opinions.|His face probably changes every time he watches them together.''')
add('sea_mysteries','LilycoveCity_House4_Text_MysteriesAtBottomOfSea','A resident repeats an uncertain claim that the planets biggest mysteries lie undersea.','''soft_smile~Hard to check the biggest mystery when it is sitting under all that water.|A plausible place for unanswered questions, though the ranking needs evidence.|Plenty down there we cannot see. Worth respecting.|I like that they left room to be unsure.|The sea still keeps plenty beyond what we bring home.|A grand claim, sensibly accompanied by a small shrug.|The mysteries chose an excellent place to avoid awkward questions.|Deep water does make investigation rather complicated.|Some secrets remain simply because reaching them is difficult.|A little uncertainty suits a claim that enormous.|I would ask where they heard it before planning an expedition.''')
add('underwater_trench','LilycoveCity_House4_Text_UnderwaterTrenchMossdeepSootopolis','A resident passes along a report of a trench between Mossdeep and Sootopolis.','''surprised~A whole trench under the sea. The ocean has an extra downstairs.|Useful geographical information, though I would verify it before diving.|Good lead. Get proper bearings before heading out.|There is more beneath that crossing than I imagined.|That sounds like a place to prepare carefully before exploring.|The route between cities apparently has a rather dramatic basement.|The sea has depth beyond its already excessive depth.|A trench would make accurate mapping especially important.|The water hides the shape of the land below it.|A remarkable feature to have out of sight between two cities.|I would like to know who first told them about that crossing.''')
add('link_record','MauvilleCity_PokemonCenter_2F_Text_Youngster','A youngster explains public Colosseum records and feels embarrassed about losses.','''soft_smile~A wall cannot show how much someone learned. It is mostly good at holding numbers.|A record measures outcomes, with very little detail about improvement.|Losses happen. The wall does not get the final word.|I would find that public record a bit intimidating too.|Anyone practicing is allowed to have a rough stretch.|The scoreboard offers a notoriously incomplete biography.|The wall has never battled anyone. Its opinion is limited.|Numbers need context, especially when someone is learning.|A string of losses can still hold courage and progress.|A bad record is no reason to make someone feel small.|I would rather hear about their most memorable match.''')
add('link_fans','MossdeepCity_PokemonCenter_2F_Text_Woman5','A woman hopes many link battle wins will earn her fans.','''laughing~First win the battles, then learn to wave without dropping anything.|Repeated wins could attract attention. Sportsmanship might keep it.|Win fairly. Treat the people watching well.|I think being kind to an opponent would impress me too.|A good winner makes other people happy to cheer.|An ambitious career plan with applause already penciled in.|She has planned the admirers before the difficult part. Admirably efficient.|Consistent results and a good attitude would be a strong combination.|The people who stay often notice more than the wins.|A following is easier to keep when the manners match the talent.|I wonder what she hopes people will remember about her battles.''')

add('cycling_safety','Route110_SeasideCyclingRoadNorthEntrance_Text_GoAllOutOnCyclingRoad Route110_SeasideCyclingRoadSouthEntrance_Text_GoAllOutOnCyclingRoad','Both cycling gate attendants encourage speed with caution around others; text is byte-identical.','''laughing~Go very fast, remain very uncrashed. A sensible two-part instruction.|Speed is enjoyable with enough stopping distance and attention.|Watch the people ahead. Leave room to stop.|I would rather enjoy the ride than surprise somebody.|Fast wind, happy rider, nobody flattened. Sounds good.|A stirring invitation with an entirely reasonable collision clause.|Freedom of the road ends at the person directly in front of us.|Brakes deserve just as much appreciation as the pedals.|A good ride leaves everyone else a good day too.|Looking ahead is an excellent accessory at any speed.|The warning tells me this attendant has seen a few close calls.''')
add('flute_worker','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_FunToBlowGlassFlute','A glass workshop employee enjoys blowing a flute while the boss speaks.','''laughing~A tiny musical interruption with full workplace enthusiasm.|A fascinating experiment in how long a supervisor tolerates accompaniment.|Hope the boss has a sense of humor.|I might wait until the boss finishes. Unless they asked for a duet.|That is one way to season a workday. Possibly too loudly.|Every speech apparently deserves an unsolicited flute part.|They have found a way to be both employed and extremely noticeable.|A glass flute makes a remarkably efficient interruption device.|A little mischief, carefully carried on a breath.|Bold workplace styling. Potentially brief employment.|I am curious whether the boss has stopped noticing by now.''')
add('origin_rumor','Route119_House_Text_RumorAboutCaveOfOrigin','A resident wonders whether Pokemon spirits revive in the Cave of Origin.','''soft_smile~That is a big story for one cave to carry. I wonder who first told it.|An intriguing belief. A rumor alone cannot establish what happens there.|Old story. We should treat the place with respect.|I can understand wanting a story like that to be true.|A place tied to that much hope must mean a lot to people.|The cave has acquired a legend far larger than its entrance.|People have always asked the dark to return what they miss.|I would want to distinguish the local history from the claim itself.|Some rumors tell us what people long for as much as what they know.|That is the kind of story that changes how you enter a place.|I would listen to more than one local account before deciding.''')
add('institute_question','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_WhatWereAquasUpTo','A saved researcher thanks the player but remains puzzled by Aquas intentions.','''soft_smile~I am glad they are safe. The Aquas left a mess of questions behind.|Their objective remains unclear, but the researchers can work safely again.|They are safe. We can worry about the rest after checking everyone.|It must feel strange to be relieved and confused at once.|Getting people safe was the first thing that mattered.|A rescue completed, with the villains' reasoning still stubbornly absent.|The danger left. Its explanation apparently missed the exit.|I would check the equipment and make sure everyone is accounted for.|Relief can arrive before understanding does.|They deserve a quiet day after that interruption.|I would ask what the Aquas actually tried to reach while they were here.''')
add('safari_welcome','Route121_SafariZoneEntrance_Text_WelcomeToSafariZone','An attendant introduces Safari Zones natural habitats and Pokemon catching.','''soft_smile~Wild Pokemon in their own habitats. We are guests with very special invitations.|Observing them in their surroundings should be as rewarding as finding them.|Respect the area and the Pokemon. Good outing follows.|I would like a quiet look around before doing anything else.|A little patience will make this visit much nicer for everyone.|An invitation to adventure, with the wildlife retaining top billing.|We have entered a place where the residents owe us no conversation.|A protected habitat is worth exploring carefully.|Walk gently. There is a whole living place around the paths.|An outing works better when visitors remember whose home it is.|I would love to see which Pokemon appear when we stop rushing.''')
add('safari_lake','SafariZone_North_Text_Fisherman','A fisherman seeks unusual Water Pokemon and asks where the lake is.','''soft_smile~A Water Pokemon mission needs water. We have identified the crucial first step.|Finding the lake would certainly improve the search conditions.|Look for water first. Then a safe bank.|I hope the lake is easier to find than the rare Pokemon.|A drink for the fisherman might be useful along the way too.|A noble expedition, briefly delayed by the location of its main ingredient.|The mission is ambitious. The navigation remains a work in progress.|Water is an excellent starting requirement for this particular search.|The rarest thing right now appears to be a clear direction.|A little local guidance would suit this expedition beautifully.|I would ask which Water Pokemon they are hoping to find.''')
add('safari_trade','SafariZone_North_Text_Man','A visitor plans to catch rare Pokemon and trade with friends.','''soft_smile~Rare finds to share with friends. That makes the excitement travel farther.|Trading can let the whole group compare very different discoveries.|Good plan. Make sure each partner gets a good home.|I like that their friends are already part of the outing.|Coming back with something to share always feels nice.|The expedition has planned its triumphant reunion before its first catch.|Their friends are about to receive very lively souvenirs.|A group can explore more possibilities by sharing what each finds.|May the excitement carry kindness along with it.|A rare find feels even better when a friend appreciates it.|I wonder what their friends hope to find in return.''')
add('safari_exhausted','SafariZone_Northwest_Text_Man','A visitor reaches a remote Safari area too exhausted to catch Pokemon.','''sad~They reached the rare Pokemon and spent all their catching energy on walking.|Their travel budget appears to have been measured in stamina.|Sit down. Catch your breath before doing anything else.|That is a disappointing time to realize how tired you are.|Water and a quiet break first. The Pokemon can wait.|A triumphant arrival, followed immediately by negotiations with their legs.|The expedition has discovered the rare limit of its own enthusiasm.|The plan needed a reserve of energy for the actual destination.|Let the place come to them for a while. No need to hurry.|A rest is a perfectly respectable part of the itinerary.|They might spot something lovely just by sitting quietly here.''')
add('safari_nature','SafariZone_RestHouse_Text_FatMan','A visitor thinks feeder Pokeblocks attract Pokemon with similar natures.','''soft_smile~A snack can bring together creatures with the same opinion of that snack.|An interesting pattern. Nature and flavor preferences might be linked.|Useful tip. Watch what comes to the feeder.|That sounds like something you learn by waiting quietly.|A shared taste can make a surprisingly good introduction.|A tiny buffet with a remarkably particular guest list.|Even the wilderness has people who agree about lunch.|We could compare which visitors choose each kind of block.|The food we leave can tell us who enjoys returning.|A feeder with its own very selective clientele.|I would like to watch a few batches before guessing the pattern.''')
add('safari_fleeing','SafariZone_RestHouse_Text_PsychicM','A visitor explains that Pokeblocks especially help with Pokemon prone to flee.','''soft_smile~A snack gives the nervous ones a reason to stay for one more moment.|The benefit would be greatest when fleeing is otherwise likely.|Makes sense. Give a nervous Pokemon some space too.|A calm moment seems better than chasing after them.|A treat works best when the guest already has a reason to leave.|A tactical use of hospitality for a very brief audience.|The promise of a snack has delayed many a hasty departure.|Useful to apply the right tool to the actual problem.|Patience and a small offering can make staying feel easier.|Good advice: notice what the individual Pokemon needs.|I would watch how comfortable they seem before moving closer.''')
add('safari_closer','SafariZone_RestHouse_Text_Youngster','A youngster reports catching Pokemon without Pokeblocks by approaching closer.','''soft_smile~No snacks, still plenty of catches. Their quiet shoes deserve some credit.|Distance can affect an attempt independently of the bait used.|Move carefully. Close does not mean crowding them.|I would take the quiet approach over a sudden rush.|A patient approach can help when the treat pouch is empty.|A successful expedition with the catering department entirely absent.|They have proved that an empty snack bag need not end the day.|A useful result from changing the distance instead of the supplies.|Going gently matters more than simply going nearer.|They made the most of what they brought. Resourceful.|I wonder how they learned to judge a comfortable approach.''')
add('safari_feeder','SafariZone_South_Text_Boy','A boy explains that Pokemon gather around a feeder containing Pokeblocks.','''soft_smile~A square box that summons hungry company. I understand its appeal.|A feeding station makes the visitors easier to observe.|Good spot to wait quietly and watch.|I like that the Pokemon can choose to come over.|Set out something good and give the guests room.|A surprisingly modest box with excellent powers of invitation.|The local gathering place has a very practical attraction.|Simple container, very effective way to bring visitors together.|A patient offering can make a little place feel busy.|It seems the little square box knows how to host.|We could learn a lot by watching who arrives first.''')
add('safari_closed','SafariZone_South_Text_AreaOffLimits1 SafariZone_South_Text_AreaOffLimits2','Both Safari construction workers explain an area is closed; exact texts match.','''soft_smile~Under construction means the adventure is still getting its shoes on.|We should stay clear until the work is completed.|Closed means closed. Plenty else to see.|I would rather not interrupt people working.|We can enjoy the open part and let them finish safely.|A future adventure, currently occupied by people with actual jobs.|The unfinished area has wisely declined our visit.|We should give the crew space to finish the job.|A boundary is easy to respect when we listen to it.|An unfinished area is best viewed after the workers say it is ready.|I would be curious to see it when the work is done.''')
add('safari_no_bike','SafariZone_South_Text_Man','A visitor regrets forgetting a bike needed to explore farther into Safari Zone.','''sad~Their adventure remembered everything except its wheels. That is frustrating.|A useful reminder to check access requirements before setting out.|Stay within reach on foot. Bring the bike next time.|That is a disappointing discovery this far into the day.|There is still a good walk to enjoy where we can reach.|An expedition defeated by one conspicuously absent bicycle.|The rarest sight today is the bike they left behind.|A transport requirement is difficult to improvise around.|The nearer paths may still have something worth finding.|A bicycle would complete this particular travel arrangement.|I wonder what they have already spotted on the way in.''')
add('safari_missing_food','SafariZone_South_Text_Youngster','A youngster suspects Pokemon ate a feeder Pokeblock without being noticed.','''laughing~A mysterious disappearing snack. The suspects were very polite about it.|A reasonable explanation, though direct observation would confirm it.|Probably eaten. Quiet visitors are still visitors.|I like imagining a shy Pokemon waiting until nobody looked.|An empty feeder can be a very nice review of the food.|A tiny culinary mystery with a very plausible hungry culprit.|The unseen guests have left an elegantly empty plate.|We might catch the next visit by watching from farther away.|Some visitors only arrive when they feel unobserved.|A vanished treat can still be a successful invitation.|I would keep a little distance and watch the next one.''')
add('safari_flavors','SafariZone_Southwest_Text_Woman','A visitor wonders whether ignored Pokeblocks reflect Pokemons food preferences.','''soft_smile~Probably! I too have strong opinions about unexpected cubes of food.|Individual taste is a sensible explanation worth checking.|They have preferences. An ignored snack is an answer.|I would rather know what they enjoy than insist on my first choice.|Absolutely. A treat is only a treat if the eater likes it.|A rejected offering need not be a rejection of the entire friendship.|The Pokemon have declined the chef's suggestion without comment.|Different blocks could help test whether the flavor is the issue.|Even a small creature can have a very firm opinion.|Taste is personal. The presentation cannot solve everything.|I would compare what that same Pokemon chooses next time.''')
add('museum_ship','SlateportCity_OceanicMuseum_2F_Text_RemindsMeOfAbandonedShip','A museum model reminds a visitor of the Abandoned Ship near Dewford.','''soft_smile~A little model brought back a very big ship. Memories fit in odd places.|A familiar shape can make a distant place feel quite immediate.|That wreck would leave an impression.|I wonder which detail made them think of it.|Seeing the model must bring the real ship to mind so clearly.|A small exhibit has opened the door to a much larger story.|One tidy model, one rather less tidy memory of a ship.|It would be interesting to compare the model's design with the wreck.|Sometimes an object carries us somewhere else for a moment.|The model seems to have earned a second, more personal meaning.|I would ask whether they had seen the Abandoned Ship up close.''')
add('museum_no_running','SlateportCity_OceanicMuseum_2F_Text_DontRunInMuseum','An adult sternly warns against running in the museum.','''flustered~Walking feet! My feet have received the message very clearly.|A reasonable rule around fragile displays and other visitors.|Slow down. We are indoors around fragile displays.|I think the whole room heard that warning.|Easy steps. Nobody wants an exhibit or a visitor knocked over.|Our tour has acquired an emphatically stated speed limit.|The museum has chosen a remarkably effective alarm system.|Fragile objects and fast feet are a poor combination.|A quieter pace leaves more room to notice things.|Graceful walking is the correct look for this room.|I suspect they have already stopped someone doing exactly that today.''')
add('museum_submarine','SlateportCity_OceanicMuseum_2F_Text_WantToRideSubmarine','A child admires a submarine and wishes to ride in one.','''soft_smile~A boat with an extra down button. I understand the excitement.|A submarine offers a rather different view of familiar water.|It would be quite a ride. With a proper crew.|Looking through a little window underwater sounds extraordinary.|I would pack lunch that stays put when the boat moves.|An adventure beginning with the bold decision to go beneath the scenery.|A wonderfully enclosed way to visit a very large unknown.|I would want to see the controls almost as much as the water.|The hidden part of the sea makes a powerful invitation.|A remarkable view, provided the cabin has a decent window.|I would love to hear what they imagine seeing down there.''')
add('ship_building','SlateportCity_SternsShipyard_2F_Text_ShipDesignMoreLikeBuilding','A designer compares a large ship to a building rather than a simple vehicle.','''surprised~A building that floats away. I would definitely label the front door.|The scale brings structural and living-space problems together.|A lot of people depend on every part holding up.|It must feel strange to design rooms that travel.|A galley has to feed a whole little moving neighborhood.|A ship is apparently a town with a departure schedule.|A building that leaves is an unusually assertive architectural choice.|Structure, space, movement, balance. That is a wonderful design challenge.|Rooms on water must make home feel a little different.|Every room has to look right and survive going somewhere.|I would like to see how they fit everyday life inside that hull.''')
add('ship_buoyancy','SlateportCity_SternsShipyard_2F_Text_FloatsBecauseBuoyancy','A worker explains that buoyancy keeps iron ships afloat.','''surprised~Iron can float if you give it the right shape. My spoon feels underambitious.|The hull displaces enough water to support its total weight. Quite elegant.|Heavy does not always mean sinking. Shape matters.|It still feels a little magical watching one move.|A heavy pot can float too, until you give it the wrong filling.|An immense iron ship, politely supported by displaced water.|The sea will hold a building if the building asks correctly.|A brilliant reminder that the entire shape matters more than the material alone.|The water carries what seems too heavy, given the right form.|An impressive silhouette with a very practical reason behind it.|I would enjoy watching someone explain it with a little model.''')

add('cozy_thanks','Cozy_Text_GardenThanks','A gardener thanks the player for a berry housewarming gift for a shrub.','''laughing~A house with mostly roots! At least it will never forget where it lives.|A generous welcome for a plant that cannot formally accept it.|Shrub got its welcome. Everyone seems pleased.|That is a sweet amount of fuss over a little plant.|A berry and a welcome. A very small housewarming feast.|The newest resident has accepted our gift through dignified silence.|A rooted household is admirably resistant to moving-day chaos.|A house with its foundations already growing. Clever.|A gentle welcome offered to something newly planted.|A charming housewarming, with excellent natural decor.|I think the neighbors enjoyed giving it a proper arrival.''')
add('cozy_decline','Cozy_Text_GardenDecline','The gardener accepts a refused berry trade and praises the shrubs patience.','''soft_smile~The shrub is extremely patient. It has not checked the time once.|Plants do make exceptionally patient recipients of delayed arrangements.|No pressure from the gardener or the shrub.|I appreciate being allowed to say no so easily.|The berry can wait. They were kind about it.|Our refusal has been met with exemplary botanical grace.|The shrub has a remarkably calm negotiating style.|No urgent deadline on this particular welcome project.|A little patience looks very natural in a garden.|They accepted that gracefully. So, apparently, did the shrub.|It is nice that the exchange stays friendly either way.''')
add('cozy_no_berry','Cozy_Text_NoBerry','Without an Oran Berry, the gardeners offer the shrub encouraging words.','''laughing~I can help with encouraging words. Nice leaves! Very leafy!|The nutritional value is limited, but the enthusiasm is considerable.|No berry today. The shrub still gets company.|Encouraging words are an unexpectedly sweet backup plan.|We can bring a berry another time. Kind words are ready now.|The pantry is empty, but the welcome speech remains fully funded.|May the shrub thrive on praise and a sensible amount of water.|Words do not replace water, but they improve the gardening atmosphere.|Speak kindly, then remember the soil needs care too.|A compliment costs nothing and suits a new arrival.|I would love to know which encouraging words they settled on.''')
add('cozy_done','Cozy_Text_GardenDone','The gardener interprets a silent shrubs silence as neighborhood approval.','''laughing~No complaints from the shrub. A flawless neighborhood review.|An encouraging interpretation, though the shrub has not supplied much evidence.|Quiet neighbor. Hard to argue with that.|I think they really wanted the shrub to feel at home.|It has settled in without a single complaint about the cooking.|A glowing review, translated freely from complete silence.|Silence is a very convenient language for an optimistic gardener.|I would also check the leaves before declaring the move successful.|A quiet arrival can still take root beautifully.|The neighborhood has apparently passed its botanical inspection.|They seem happy enough with the new resident for both of them.''')
add('cozy_helper','Cozy_Text_GardenHelper','A helper labels a shrub HELLO I AM A SHRUB so it feels seen.','''laughing~A name tag! Good. I would hate to call the shrub Mister Hedge by mistake.|Taxonomically broad, socially welcoming. An efficient little sign.|Nobody can say the shrub was overlooked.|That is wonderfully earnest. I rather like it.|A welcome sign makes even a small garden feel cared for.|Our leafy newcomer has received an exceptionally clear introduction.|At last, a label that makes no unreasonable demands of its subject.|Clear lettering, accurate description. Excellent sign design.|Being noticed can be a very small and tender gift.|A little literal, but the intention is beautifully styled.|I think the person who made it needed the introduction too.''')
add('cozy_welcome_gift','Cozy_Text_WelcomeGift','A welcoming neighbor gives a Potion instead of the helpers proposed shrub.','''laughing~A Potion is easier to carry. The shrub would want a window seat.|A practical gift, with a sensible limit on unsolicited horticulture.|Potion is useful. Leave the shrub planted.|The thought behind both gifts is rather lovely.|A Potion travels better than a shrub. Good compromise.|A warm welcome, rescued from becoming a major landscaping commitment.|We narrowly avoided acquiring a dependent with photosynthesis.|Portability seems like an excellent requirement for a travel gift.|The shrub may be happier staying rooted while we go.|A thoughtful gift with considerably less soil in the bag.|They clearly talked this through. Possibly more than once.''')
add('cozy_welcome_again','Cozy_Text_WelcomeAgain','A neighbor proudly gives an unrehearsed welcome back.','''soft_smile~A spontaneous welcome! Quick, applaud before they start taking notes.|An unrehearsed result with excellent warmth and timing.|Good to be welcomed back without a script.|It sounded natural. That made it nicer.|The welcome is the part that matters, practiced or otherwise.|A flawless improvisation from our increasingly experienced hosts.|Spontaneity has been carefully identified after the fact.|Nice to see the welcome procedure working without preparation.|Familiar kindness does not need rehearsing every time.|An effortless welcome, proudly presented as effortless.|They seemed pleased to greet us before thinking about how.''')
add('cozy_committee','Cozy_Text_WelcomeHelper','A former solo welcome committee now takes meeting minutes mostly about shrubs.','''laughing~Official shrub minutes! Was the shrub present, or merely well represented?|A growing committee with a surprisingly stable research subject.|Two people, several minutes, one very discussed shrub.|I like how a small welcome became something they do together.|A committee should at least get some tea with those shrub discussions.|Local government has discovered its first great leafy controversy.|Bureaucracy arrived quietly, then requested a separate shrub agenda.|The scope grew from greeting people to managing botanical records.|Two neighbors found something small to tend together.|The shrub has acquired a truly remarkable support staff.|I would be curious to read just one set of those minutes.''')
add('cozy_bag_full','Cozy_Text_BagFull','A neighbor offers to hold a gift until the players bag has room.','''soft_smile~They will keep it safe. My bag needs a small internal town meeting.|No urgency, then. A little inventory space will resolve this.|They can hold it. Sort the bag when we have a moment.|That was kind. No need to rush it.|A gift kept for later is still a lovely offer.|Our generosity problem has been postponed by a very full bag.|The bag has declined further responsibility for the afternoon.|A small storage adjustment and we can complete the exchange.|The kindness will still be here when there is room.|We have reached the point where the bag needs editing.|They made a full bag feel like a simple delay.''')

add('swagger_decline','MoveTutor_Text_SwaggerDeclined','The Swagger tutor protests that the player will not get into the spirit.','''laughing~I can appreciate the spirit without signing up for extra swagger.|Declining a move is not necessarily a failure of enthusiasm.|We said no. The swagger lesson can wait.|I think I have enough trouble standing confidently already.|Some days a little quiet confidence is plenty.|Our refusal has failed the instructor's entirely subjective spirit test.|My spirit prefers to remain seated and faintly unimpressed.|Enthusiasm and move selection can be separate decisions.|A loud invitation can still receive a quiet answer.|Swagger is a choice, darling. Let us choose.|I wonder whether they greet every refusal with that same challenge.''')
add('swagger_taught','MoveTutor_Text_SwaggerTaught','After teaching Swagger, the tutor resolves to praise their Pokemon without swaggering.','''soft_smile~Good plan. The Pokemon gets the compliment without a side order of showing off.|Praise can be clear and sincere without the extra performance.|Give the partner credit. That is enough.|A simple compliment can be easier to believe.|Kind words do not need much dressing up.|The master of Swagger has discovered the power of a straightforward compliment.|An unexpectedly restrained ending from the swagger department.|A simpler method with fewer opportunities for confusion.|Honest affection can stand quite well on its own.|Praise looks best when it fits the person receiving it.|That sounds like a nice change their Pokemon might notice.''')
add('rollout_decline','MoveTutor_Text_RolloutDeclined','The Rollout tutor mistakes a declined lesson for shyness and urges rolling.','''flustered~I am not shy about rolling. I just prefer knowing where I will stop.|The decision may involve considerations other than reluctance.|No lesson today. Mind where you roll.|I can be shy and still have made a decision.|We can admire the enthusiasm from a stable position.|A simple refusal has somehow been diagnosed as insufficient rolling.|My reserve has been mistaken for an unmet need to tumble.|I would want a clear path before endorsing this plan.|It is all right to enjoy the grass without becoming a wheel.|That is a very persistent invitation to ruin one's hem.|They do seem determined to share their favorite activity.''')
add('rollout_taught','MoveTutor_Text_RolloutTaught','The Rollout tutor says rolling in grass makes them happy and invites company.','''laughing~A grass roll does sound fun. We should check for rocks before becoming wheels.|An uncomplicated source of happiness. Clear ground would improve it.|Watch for stones first. Then enjoy yourself.|That sounds silly in quite a nice way.|A little clean grass is a lovely place for a break.|An open invitation to abandon dignity in a pleasant meadow.|Happiness has apparently been lying sideways in the grass all along.|Low equipment requirements. I can appreciate a simple activity.|Sometimes the earth is best greeted at ground level.|Fun first, then a thorough inspection for grass stains.|I would like to know who joined in before we arrived.''')
add('fury_decline','MoveTutor_Text_FuryCutterDeclined','The Fury Cutter tutor says the player is on another wavelength after a refusal.','''soft_smile~Different wavelengths, same perfectly usable conversation. We said no nicely.|A difference in move preference need not imply a deeper incompatibility.|Different choice. Nothing wrong with that.|Not every quiet answer means we misunderstood.|We can like the person without choosing the same thing.|An entire philosophical divide inferred from one declined lesson.|Our frequencies have failed to synchronize over a move choice.|Two workable plans can use different settings.|A difference can stay small if we let it.|It is possible to disagree without making it the whole outfit.|I think the answer was clearer than their reaction suggests.''')
add('fury_taught','MoveTutor_Text_FuryCutterTaught','The Fury Cutter tutor enjoys the suspense of consecutive hits.','''surprised~One hit, then another! A very sharp way to keep everybody counting.|A sequence does create suspense as the successful hits accumulate.|Keeping it going takes focus. Watch the opening.|I can see why everyone would hold their breath.|There is a certain satisfaction when careful repetition works.|The thrill lies in whether the next stroke joins the last.|An increasingly pointed lesson in anticipation.|A chain of successful actions is satisfying to watch.|The small question returns with every movement.|Consistency gives the whole performance its impact.|I would watch the Pokemon's timing as much as the result.''')
add('mimic_decline','MoveTutor_MimicDeclined','The Mimic tutor is disappointed not to teach the players Pokemon.','''soft_smile~They really wanted a student. Maybe another Pokemon will enjoy the lesson.|A disappointed instructor, but the move should still suit the learner.|No lesson today. They can offer again another time.|I feel a little bad, but declining was still allowed.|A willing student will make a better lesson for everyone.|A planned lesson has lost its leading pupil before rehearsals began.|The tutor's enthusiasm has briefly outrun the enrollment.|A good offer can still be the wrong fit for this partner.|There will be another chance to share that skill.|Enthusiasm is lovely. A little grace with refusal helps too.|I wonder which Pokemon they would most enjoy teaching.''')
add('mimic_taught','MoveTutor_Text_MimicTaught','The Mimic tutor praises the moves depth and challenges the players ability to copy.','''laughing~Can I copy them perfectly? I would start by copying that very confident face.|Imitation can require careful observation rather than simple repetition.|Good lesson. Practice before boasting about it.|I would rather learn carefully than claim I had it already.|Getting the little details right often takes more patience.|The instructor has left us with both a lesson and a competitive wink.|An invitation to copy someone who clearly enjoys being the original.|I would need to watch the motion several times before trying it.|Looking closely can reveal how much a simple act contains.|A convincing imitation depends on the details people overlook.|I would ask them to demonstrate once more, if they would.''')
add('metronome_decline','MoveTutor_Text_MetronomeDeclined','The Metronome tutor leaves a declined offer open for later.','''soft_smile~A friendly offer with no ticking clock. Very considerate for a Metronome tutor.|A useful option we can revisit without pressure.|We know where to find them. Good.|I appreciate that they let the answer stand.|A kind offer can wait until it suits the partner.|The invitation remains open, with admirable absence of dramatic protest.|An uncomplicated refusal accepted. A small luxury.|We can return if our plans change. Nice and practical.|Some doors stay open without anyone pulling us through.|They handled that with excellent manners.|It is good to leave a conversation welcome to continue.''')
add('metronome_taught','MoveTutor_Text_MetronomeTaught','The tutor imagines humans using Metronome by waggling a finger.','''laughing~I have waggled a finger. So far it mostly summons questions about my finger.|An entertaining possibility with a rather unpredictable range of outcomes.|Maybe practice somewhere with plenty of space.|I think I would be nervous about what came next.|I would prefer my kitchen tools to keep doing the same thing.|A grand ambition, resting on one extremely unassuming finger.|I enjoy surprises more when they cannot alter the furniture.|Random outputs would make for an unusually difficult control test.|A small motion should not be trusted with every possible consequence.|The gesture is charming. The unknown result might be less so.|I would watch from a comfortable distance for the first attempt.''')
add('sleep_talk_decline','MoveTutor_Text_SleepTalkDeclined','The Sleep Talk tutor accepts refusal by relating it to staying awake with Hidden Power.','''soft_smile~Staying awake is my main technique for knowing what I am saying.|An understandable preference. Sleep and deliberate choices do not overlap reliably.|Awake works for us today. No harm done.|I am awkward enough when I can hear my own words.|There is something to be said for choosing when to take a nap.|Our wakefulness has received an oddly elaborate interpretation.|I prefer my embarrassing remarks fully conscious and properly regrettable.|Conscious control remains a very useful feature.|The waking world has enough surprises for one afternoon.|A perfectly respectable choice, even without that explanation.|They have managed to connect our refusal to their favorite subject.''')
add('sleep_talk_taught','MoveTutor_Text_SleepTalkTaught','The Sleep Talk tutor hopes to get their wifes coin trick right even while asleep.','''laughing~Maybe the sleeping guess will surprise them both. The coin has been winning.|If the trick is fair, another state of wakefulness will not improve the odds.|Coin is still a coin. Keep the stakes small.|That is a strangely sweet ambition to share.|I hope they both get a good laugh out of the next try.|A modest marital triumph pursued through increasingly unusual methods.|They have exhausted waking guesses and moved to the night shift.|We should check how the coin trick works before redesigning the guesser.|Some little shared games matter more than the answer.|Their wife's winning streak has inspired remarkable dedication.|I would like to hear how long the two of them have played that trick.''')
add('substitute_decline','MoveTutor_Text_SubstituteDeclined','The Substitute tutor responds to refusal by explaining that Pokemon can create copies.','''surprised~A copy does sound useful. It still does not have to be today's lesson.|A notable capability, though suitability remains a separate question.|Useful move. Still our choice to pass.|I would want to understand it before choosing it.|An interesting offer can wait for the right partner.|The declined proposal has returned with an additional selling point.|A second version of oneself sounds like twice the questions.|I have plenty of questions, but none changes the answer yet.|Even an unusual gift should be offered without pulling.|A copy is intriguing. The original still gets the decision.|I think they are surprised we were not immediately convinced.''')
add('substitute_taught','MoveTutor_Text_SubstituteTaught','The Substitute tutor urges humans to enjoy their own lives fully.','''soft_smile~A good reminder. My own life does include some excellent ordinary afternoons.|A worthwhile conclusion from an unexpectedly unusual lesson.|Enjoy the time you have. Make it count.|I like a quiet good day as much as a grand one.|Good company and something warm to eat count for plenty.|An unusually generous parting instruction: live a life worth enjoying.|I shall enjoy mine at a comfortable volume, where possible.|There is a lot worth making and trying while we are here.|A life can be full without every moment being loud.|Enjoying your own life is a very personal kind of good taste.|I would be interested in what an ideal day looks like for them.''')
add('dynamic_decline','MoveTutor_Text_DynamicPunchDeclined','The DynamicPunch tutor angrily takes refusal as mockery.','''flustered~Nobody is making fun! Please keep the punch demonstration aimed away from us.|The refusal was not an insult. We should keep a sensible distance.|We declined a lesson. Back up a step.|That got loud very quickly. I would like some space.|A no should not have to come with reassurance about punching.|The sales pitch has developed an unnecessarily aggressive second act.|I prefer my declined offers without accompanying impacts.|That is not encouraging feedback for a potential student.|An angry motion can make a small disagreement feel very large.|That reaction has certainly not improved the offer.|I would stop trying to explain until they have calmed down.''')
add('dynamic_taught','MoveTutor_Text_DynamicPunchTaught','The DynamicPunch tutor hopes the player will win at Mossdeep Gym using the move.','''soft_smile~A very specific wish for our new punch. We will choose our moment.|We should weigh the move against the actual opponents before deciding.|We will use what fits the match. Thanks for the lesson.|They sound eager to hear how it turns out.|A new technique helps most when it suits the partner using it.|The lesson comes with a suggested triumphant destination.|Our instructor has already imagined the victory in impressive detail.|Another option for the team. We can plan around its strengths.|A taught skill still needs a thoughtful hand guiding it.|We should choose the moment that makes the move look its best.|I wonder whether they ask every student to report back.''')
add('double_edge_decline','MoveTutor_Text_DoubleEdgeDeclined','The Double-Edge tutor feels personally rejected after a declined lesson.','''sad~We declined a move, not them. I wish that difference hurt a little less.|An unsuitable lesson does not make the instructor unwanted.|It is the move we passed on. Nothing personal.|Oh. That sounded like it landed on an older hurt.|I would say it gently. They seem to be having a rough day.|A practical refusal has stumbled into a much more personal story.|That little word even is carrying an unfortunate amount of history.|The offer and the person are different things. I hope they hear that.|A small answer can touch a bruise we did not know was there.|A little kindness would suit the moment better than a sharp reply.|I would make sure they knew we were not dismissing them.''')
add('double_edge_taught','MoveTutor_Text_DoubleEdgeTaught','After teaching Double-Edge, the tutor resolves to become tough instead of living for love.','''sad~They can get stronger without throwing away every soft part. Soft parts matter.|Strength need not require giving up the capacity for affection.|Get stronger. Do not turn it into punishment.|I hope they leave room to feel differently later.|They deserve care even while learning to stand on their own.|A wounded heart has announced a rather severe new training plan.|Being tough still leaves room for an inconvenient heart.|A sturdier plan does not need to remove every gentle feature.|The hurting part does not have to decide the whole future.|Strength can look softer than they seem to expect.|I would like to know they have someone kind to talk to.''')
add('explosion_decline','MoveTutor_Text_ExplosionDeclined','The Explosion tutor assumes a refused lesson is prejudice against country life.','''flustered~The countryside is fine! We are allowed a small opinion about Explosion.|Their address is irrelevant to whether the move suits a partner.|Nothing to do with the country. We passed on the move.|I wish the refusal had not made them feel looked down on.|Country kitchens are lovely. This really is just a move choice.|Our tactical decision has accidentally become a rural grievance.|The countryside has been dragged into an entirely separate disagreement.|Location did not enter the calculation. The move did.|A place can matter deeply without causing every answer.|No insult to country living was included in that refusal.|I wonder how often someone has made them feel that way before.''')
add('explosion_taught','MoveTutor_Text_ExplosionTaught','The Explosion tutor realizes they may stay because they actually want country life.','''soft_smile~Maybe staying is the choice, then. The countryside does not need exploding.|Recognizing their own preference is more useful than forcing a dramatic change.|If they like it here, they can stay. Simple enough.|That sounds like a small honest thing they needed to say.|Liking the life you already have is a perfectly good reason.|The long-awaited grand departure has met a persuasive fondness for home.|A life does not need an explosion to prove it happened.|No redesign needed if the place already meets their needs.|Some roots hold because we want them to.|Staying can be a deliberate choice with excellent taste.|I like that they finally allowed themself that possibility.''')

add('scarf_no_room','DewfordTown_House2_Text_NoRoom','A scarf enthusiast says they would sell every item to make space for the Silk Scarf.','''laughing~I respect the scarf, but I would like to keep at least one useful pocket.|A strong preference for fashion over inventory diversity.|We can make room without selling everything.|That is a startling amount of devotion to one scarf.|I would keep the lunch and make room another way.|A passionate defense of the scarf as the only truly necessary possession.|One scarf against the entire bag. The scarf has a determined advocate.|A smaller inventory adjustment should solve this problem.|We need not empty our life to welcome one lovely thing.|A stunning scarf deserves space. Perhaps not every single possession.|I wonder how many other scarves they already own.''')
add('scarf_explanation','DewfordTown_House2_Text_ExplainSilkScarf','A resident explains the Silk Scarf boosts Normal moves and suits most Pokemon.','''soft_smile~Stylish AND helpful. The scarf is putting in an excellent day's work.|A versatile accessory with a specific benefit for Normal-type moves.|Useful gift. Give it to a partner who can use it.|I like something practical that still looks nice.|A thoughtful little extra for the right partner.|An accessory with both an aesthetic argument and a tactical one.|At last, fabric willing to contribute more than mysterious laundry.|A wearable improvement that does not require a complicated mechanism.|A soft little gift with a useful purpose.|Good drape, wide appeal, and an actual benefit. Excellent scarf.|I would like to see which partner it suits best.''')
add('contest_spouse','LilycoveCity_ContestHall_Text_ComeOnDear','A spouse cheers their partners Pokemon as the best.','''soft_smile~That is a cheer with years of affection behind it.|Their confidence in their partner is pleasantly unmistakable.|Good support. Let them hear it.|That is such a warm thing to hear from the audience.|Someone important is cheering them on. That matters.|The most important critic has already delivered a glowing review.|An admirably biased and entirely sincere assessment.|A little encouragement can steady a whole performance.|Love has a very clear favorite in this room.|Loyalty is always a lovely thing to wear openly.|I would watch the contestant's face when that cheer reaches them.''')
add('contest_later','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_ParticipateAnotherTime','A contest receptionist politely welcomes participation another time.','''soft_smile~No contest today, still invited tomorrow. That is a nice way to leave.|A courteous end to the arrangement. The option remains available.|Another time works. We know where to come.|I appreciate the lack of fuss about waiting.|We can return when the partner is ready for it.|Our deferred debut has been received with admirable courtesy.|The contest will survive our absence for one afternoon.|A plan can be postponed without needing to be abandoned.|There is comfort in an invitation that leaves room.|They kept the welcome intact even as we left.|That makes coming back feel quite easy.''')
add('contest_case_child','LilycoveCity_ContestLobby_Text_LadyGaveMePokeblockCase','A child celebrates receiving a Pokeblock Case from reception.','''soft_smile~A proper home for tiny snacks! The child has identified the best news.|A useful case and a very happy recipient.|Good. Now the blocks have somewhere to go.|That little gift clearly made their day.|A snack case is a wonderful reason for a small celebration.|The day's greatest treasure has turned out to be a box for treats.|An empty case can hold an astonishing amount of anticipation.|A dedicated container is a genuinely useful improvement.|A kind gesture can be big news to someone small.|The case has arrived before the collection. Excellent preparation.|I wonder what they plan to put in it first.''')
add('scott_sleepy','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_SnoozingPreferBattles','Scott wakes from a nap, prefers battles but encourages enjoying Hoenns different events.','''laughing~He inspected the contest through closed eyelids. At least the advice is awake now.|An honest preference, with a welcome willingness to recommend other activities.|He likes battles. Good that he lets others enjoy the rest.|I like that he admitted the nap instead of pretending.|Trying different things is part of what makes travel good.|A sleeping critic awakens to deliver a surprisingly generous review.|He has assessed the entertainment and the quality of the available nap.|Different challenges exercise different skills. Plenty worth trying.|His favorite path need not be the only pleasant one.|A purist who still lets other people have taste. How refreshing.|I would be curious what caught his interest before he nodded off.''')
add('scott_strategy','LilycoveCity_CoveLilyMotel_2F_Text_ContestsDoTakeStrategy','Scott recognizes contest strategy as a way to improve as a trainer.','''soft_smile~Different challenge, still using the thinking parts. Good thinking gets around.|Planning for another scoring system can broaden a trainer's judgment.|Learning another approach can help. Worth considering.|I like seeing someone reconsider a thing outside their favorite.|A new kind of challenge can teach a familiar partner something.|The battle enthusiast has found a respectable bridge to contests.|He has allowed the contest to have an actual thought in it.|Working under different constraints is excellent practice.|A path we did not favor can still teach us something.|Strategy wears more than one style of victory.|I would ask what contest tactic first changed his mind.''')
add('sleep_health','LilycoveCity_House2_Text_SleepIsEssential','A sleepy resident emphasizes rest and recovery.','''soft_smile~A very convincing sleep recommendation. The yawn did half the explaining.|Rest is a sensible part of recovery, even during an adventure.|Sleep when you need it. Tired mistakes add up.|That yawn nearly convinced me to have one too.|A good meal helps. So does actually getting enough sleep.|A health lecture delivered from the edge of an excellent nap.|They make a compelling argument for becoming temporarily unavailable.|Even a busy day needs time to stop and recover.|The quiet hours do their own kind of useful work.|Rest improves almost everything about the next morning.|I think we should let them follow their own advice.''')
add('family_pokeblock_advice','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_ExplainPokeblocks','A mother explains smooth low-feel high-level Pokeblocks and values partners, cooperation and family.','''soft_smile~That was a whole recipe for snacks and happiness. Quite a generous serving.|Detailed advice on quality, followed by a humane explanation of why it matters.|Good advice. Work together and look after your partners.|The part about a loving family stayed with me.|Good ingredients, good company, and care. I like her recipe.|A technical lesson that quietly became a small manifesto for happiness.|A long explanation with an unexpectedly warm center.|The process works better with different berries and more people. Nice.|She placed the little cubes inside a much larger picture of care.|Smooth results begin with good choices and willing collaborators.|She clearly learned more than just the mechanics of blending.''')
add('family_advice_decline','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_OhAreYouSure','A mother accepts refusal of advice but warns against doing everything alone.','''soft_smile~We passed on the lecture, not the whole idea of having help.|Independence and accepting useful advice are quite compatible.|We can ask later. No need to do everything alone.|I know the urge to manage quietly. Help is still nice.|Another pair of hands can make an ordinary day easier.|A refused explanation has left one rather good final sentence.|Solitude is pleasant. Carrying every task alone is less so.|Collaboration saves a lot of solving the same problem twice.|There is room to choose help without losing your own way.|Asking for advice does not spoil an otherwise independent look.|She seems more concerned about us than about finishing the explanation.''')
add('quad_multi','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_GoingToWinMultiBattles','One quadruplet confidently expects to win the familys Multi Battles.','''laughing~Confidence is doing warm-up laps before the battle even starts.|A bold forecast. A team event has more than one decision-maker.|Work with your teammate. That helps more than announcing the win.|That sounds like a familiar argument in this house.|A bit of friendly competition can make family time lively.|A victory speech has been prepared before the first turn.|The household has at least one self-appointed champion.|Coordination will be the interesting part of that plan.|Confidence is brighter when there is room for a teammate.|A bold little declaration. I wonder what the others think.|I would like to hear the same prediction from their partner.''')
add('quad_record','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_LikeMixingAtRecordCorner','A child enjoys mixing at the Record Corner without understanding what is mixed.','''laughing~Mystery mixing! I would at least check whether a spoon is involved.|Enjoying a process can certainly precede understanding its contents.|Worth asking what is being shared before starting.|That is an honest little question. I like it.|I usually want to know what is going into the mix.|A devoted participant in a procedure of entirely uncertain meaning.|Enthusiasm has arrived well ahead of the explanation.|That is exactly the question to ask before pressing the button.|Curiosity is a good next step after enjoying something.|A little clarity would complete this very enthusiastic picture.|I wonder what they thought was being mixed the first time.''')
add('quad_blocks','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_MakePokeblocksWithBerryBlender','A child plans super Pokeblocks with the Berry Blender.','''soft_smile~Super snacks are a noble family project. I can supervise the cheering.|A promising group experiment, provided everyone keeps good timing.|Good plan. Pay attention to the timing.|They sound eager enough to fill the whole case.|Good berries and everyone working together should help.|An ambitious culinary production with an appropriately small final product.|The family is preparing to cube its enthusiasm.|A fun way to see teamwork make an immediate difference.|Small shared projects can leave lovely memories.|Super results deserve a little care with the ingredients.|I would love to see the whole group at the blender.''')
add('quad_tough','LilycoveCity_House3_Text_GoingToEnterContest','A child wants to show off their Pokemons toughness in a contest.','''soft_smile~A contest is a very organized way to say look at my excellent friend.|A suitable place to demonstrate the quality they admire.|Let the partner show what it can do.|It is sweet how proud they sound of their Pokemon.|Sharing that pride can be part of the fun.|The boast has found itself a proper venue and a judging panel.|A public announcement of toughness, now with formal scoring.|Choose appeals that show the strength they already enjoy.|Affection can be a very eager little voice.|A fitting place to put that confidence on display.|I wonder which appeal they cannot wait to show everyone.''')

add('briney_deliveries_wait','Route104_MrBrineysHouse_Text_DeclineDeliverySail','Mr Briney accepts postponing the delivery voyage and remains available.','''soft_smile~The boat can wait while we get ready. Nice to have a patient captain.|A flexible departure is useful when carrying someone else's parcel.|We will be ready before we sail. Good.|I appreciate not being hurried onto the boat.|Time to check supplies before setting off with the delivery.|Our voyage has been granted a brief and agreeable postponement.|The sea has not left, and neither has the captain.|A useful chance to make sure nothing important was forgotten.|A willing boatman makes the coming crossing feel gentler.|A gracious delay is better than a rushed departure.|He sounds ready to help whenever we return.''')
add('briney_peeko_debt','Route104_MrBrineysHouse_Text_TellMeWheneverYouWantToSail','Mr Briney gratefully offers future passage because the player saved Peeko.','''soft_smile~Peeko is safe, and we have a grateful captain. A very good ending.|A generous offer rooted in a rescue that mattered deeply to him.|Glad Peeko is all right. We can sail when ready.|You can hear how much that little bird means to him.|Helping his friend meant more than any fare could.|A rescue has opened a sea route through simple, heartfelt gratitude.|His passenger list has acquired a rather tender exception.|A reliable crossing and a thankful friend. Good connections to have.|One small life can matter as much as a whole voyage.|A lovely offer from someone whose dearest companion came home.|I would remember the way he spoke about Peeko.''')
add('berry_regrowth','Route104_PrettyPetalFlowerShop_Text_WailmerPailExplanation','A florist explains watering berries and dropped berries sprouting again.','''soft_smile~The berries plant their own replacements. Very committed little fruit.|Dropped seeds continuing the cycle is a lovely thing to notice.|Water them. Pick what you need. Let the rest grow.|I like that a missed harvest can become another beginning.|A little care now can mean fruit to share later.|The berry has found a way to turn a missed collection into a sequel.|Neglected fruit has apparently developed a sensible backup plan.|A system that can restart itself is quite impressive.|What falls can take root, given enough time and care.|A little water keeps the whole growing arrangement beautiful.|I would enjoy returning to see what sprouted after the old crop fell.''')
add('berry_candy','Route104_PrettyPetalFlowerShop_Text_MachineMixesBerries','A flower shop resident describes berry uses and wants some of the Pokemon candy.','''laughing~At last, somebody asks the important question: what about our candy?|Many uses for one fruit. Their personal interest is quite understandable.|Fair question. They should make a batch for people too.|I would be curious about the taste myself.|I respect a fellow traveler toward the snack question.|A wide-ranging botanical lecture has arrived at its true motive.|The educational explanation has quietly become a request for sweets.|A berry-mixing machine sounds useful to more than its intended customers.|Fruit can feed a plant, a partner, and a very human hope.|An informative speech with a delightfully honest sweet tooth.|I wonder what flavor they imagine the candy would have.''')
add('mr_sea_intro','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_SeashoreHouseIntro','Mr Sea introduces his battle house and offers rewards for defeating its trainers.','''laughing~A whole house powered by enthusiastic battles. The soda must work overtime.|A clear challenge with a promised reward for completing the group.|We know the terms. Check the team before starting.|That welcome was almost hotter than the beach.|Hot battles and something cold afterward sound like his whole plan.|Our host has introduced himself, his passion, and the afternoon's challenge.|The establishment has a very specific source of indoor heating.|Three matches make a proper test of how well the team holds up.|His joy in the place is difficult to miss.|A host who knows exactly what experience he wants to offer.|I would like to hear what made him start this house.''')
add('mr_sea_hot','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_ShowMeSomeHotMatches','Mr Sea says he runs the house solely for exciting battles.','''laughing~He did not open a quiet reading room by accident, that is certain.|The house has a remarkably focused statement of purpose.|He wants a good match. We can respect that.|His enthusiasm has not cooled at all.|He knows what brings him joy and built a place for it.|A proprietor entirely free of ambiguity about his audience expectations.|One ambition, pursued at an admirably warm temperature.|A very specialized venue with a clearly satisfied operator.|Some people make a place around the thing they love.|A strong concept, delivered with completely consistent branding.|I think he enjoys watching just as much as anyone battling.''')
add('mr_sea_hold_soda','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_BagFull','Mr Sea holds the earned Soda Pop because the players bag is full.','''soft_smile~The reward is safe. Our bag just cannot absorb six more celebrations.|A simple capacity issue. The bottles can wait here.|He will hold them. Make room before coming back.|That is kind. The win still counts.|Cold soda will be welcome after we clear a little space.|Our victory has exceeded the carrying capacity of its celebration.|A bag full enough to defeat half a dozen bottles. Impressive.|Six bottles need a little planning if we want them intact.|A promised reward is still waiting kindly for us.|We can make room without turning the whole bag inside out here.|I like that he made it clear the bottles are still ours.''')
add('mr_sea_decline','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_ThatsTooBad','Mr Sea is mildly disappointed when the player declines buying Soda Pop.','''soft_smile~No soda today. The bubbles will find another audience.|A declined sale, accepted without much ceremony.|We can pass. He will be all right.|A small disappointment, quickly over.|We can choose a drink when we actually want one.|The proposed refreshment has lost its customer, with minimal tragedy.|A sale has perished quietly. The soda remains intact.|No need to carry something we do not currently need.|An offer can end gently with a simple no.|A polite refusal does not require a second purchase.|He sounds disappointed, but he let the answer stand.''')
add('mr_sea_purchase','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_HereYouGo','Mr Sea hands over a purchased bottle of Soda Pop.','''soft_smile~One bottle, safely acquired. Mind the fizz when we open it.|Purchase complete. A straightforward little exchange.|Got the drink. Put it somewhere secure.|That was quick. I hope it stays cool.|A cold drink is a lovely thing after the beach.|A brief transaction with a pleasantly fizzy conclusion.|A tiny triumph over thirst and the economics of bottles.|Keep it upright if possible. The next opening will be kinder.|A simple little kindness in the middle of a busy day.|A bottle secured without any dramatic bargaining.|He has that exchange down to a very efficient few words.''')
add('mr_sea_money','Route109_SeashoreHouse_Text_NotEnoughMoney','Mr Sea refuses a Soda Pop sale because the player lacks money.','''sad~The bottle costs more than our current pocket jingle. We can wait.|Insufficient funds, then. The purchase can be postponed.|Cannot buy it yet. Keep moving.|That is a little awkward, but easily understood.|We should keep what money we have for what we need.|The refreshment proposal has encountered a decisive financial obstacle.|Our pockets have submitted a very brief negative report.|A price check before choosing would save us the extra step.|The drink will still be here another day.|A budget is allowed to veto an accessory bottle.|A simple price and a simple answer. No guessing left.''')
add('trick_thinking','Route110_TrickHouseEntrance_Text_InMidstOfDevisingNewChallenges','The Trick Master asks for more time to devise new challenges.','''laughing~The tricks are still cooking. Best not lift the lid on his brain.|Designing a fair challenge does require time and testing.|Give him time. Better a finished puzzle.|I would not want someone hovering while I was trying to invent.|A good result sometimes needs a little longer in preparation.|Our impatient audience has interrupted the next elaborate construction.|The genius is temporarily unavailable beneath a pile of thoughts.|New puzzles need more than the first idea. Let him work.|A little absence can give an idea room to form.|We can return when the new arrangement is ready to impress.|I wonder which part of the next challenge is holding him up.''')
add('trick_reward_question','Route110_TrickHouseEntrance_Text_DidYouNotComeToClaimReward','The Trick Master is surprised the player did not come to claim the pending reward.','''soft_smile~We came without collecting? That is a very unusual treasure-hunting technique.|A pending reward is still available, apparently.|We can collect it when ready. No mystery.|He sounds surprised we stopped for anything else.|A little reward is always nicer when there is room for it.|Our host expected a collection scene and received an unscripted visit.|Even a reward can wait while we do something inexplicable.|A useful reminder that something is still waiting here.|Not every return needs to be for what we can carry away.|He has remembered the prize more carefully than we have.|I wonder what he thought we had come back to discuss.''')

add('soot_sack_explain','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_ExplainSootSack','A glassworker explains gathering volcanic ash by walking with the Soot Sack.','''soft_smile~A walk that collects tomorrow's glass. Our dusty shoes have a purpose.|A useful way to gather fine material while traveling the route.|Keep the sack with us. Watch the path.|I like knowing the ash can become something lovely.|A little gathering as we walk sounds quite manageable.|The road has become a supplier for a future piece of glass.|Our wandering has acquired a surprisingly respectable industrial function.|Collecting material through ordinary movement is a neat arrangement.|Something soft and gray can become something clear and bright.|Even dust can have an elegant second life.|I would enjoy seeing what our gathered ash eventually becomes.''')
add('soot_sack_missing','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_HaventGotYourSootSack','The glassworker points out that the player must carry the Soot Sack to collect ash.','''flustered~Right. Collecting dust requires the dust bag. That is painfully logical.|The container is necessary for accumulation. A simple thing to overlook.|Bring the sack. Then the walking counts.|At least they noticed before we took another long walk.|No sack means no saved ash. We can fix that.|Our collection expedition has misplaced its principal collecting device.|The plan has failed at the very first noun.|A system only works when the required component is actually present.|A small forgotten thing can change the whole errand.|The practical accessory turns out to be essential.|I would check the bag before heading back into the ash.''')
add('ash_decline','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_AllThatAshButDontWantAnything','A glassworker is surprised the player does not want an item despite gathering ash.','''soft_smile~The ash can wait until we know what it wants to be.|Gathering material does not require choosing its use immediately.|We can decide later. No need to rush it.|I like taking a moment before picking something.|A good ingredient can wait for the right idea.|An industrious gathering phase has been followed by artistic indecision.|Our ash is enjoying a brief period of unlimited possibilities.|We have the material. Choosing the right result is the next step.|Unmade things can wait quietly without losing their promise.|Better to choose something we love than fill a space at random.|I would like to look at the options before committing the ash.''')
add('ash_short','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_NotEnoughAshNeedX','The glassworker gives the remaining steps needed to gather enough ash for a Blue Flute.','''soft_smile~Our flute needs a little more walking before it learns to be a flute.|A precise remaining requirement. We can plan the next stretch accordingly.|More ash needed. We know how much.|At least the goal is clear now.|A bit more gathering and the batch will be ready.|The missing ingredient has been translated directly into footsteps.|Our future flute has requested additional scenic exercise.|A measurable target makes the next collection run easier.|A little more of the road will go into that music.|We can finish gathering before choosing the final place for it.|I appreciate knowing the distance still left in the errand.''')
add('glass_bag_full','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_NoRoomInBag','The glassworker holds a finished flute until the players bag has space.','''soft_smile~Finished glass deserves a safe pocket. They are right to keep it here.|A fragile item is better held safely than forced into a full bag.|Clear some space. Do not crush the new flute.|I would rather wait than hear it break in the bag.|We should make a little protected place for it.|The finished work awaits a less crowded journey to its new owner.|The bag has wisely been denied a chance to damage fresh glass.|A safe storage slot is part of getting the finished item home.|Let the delicate thing wait where it is safe.|A lovely new flute deserves better than being wedged between supplies.|It is kind of them to keep the finished piece until we are ready.''')
add('glass_decor_full','Route113_GlassWorkshop_Text_NoRoomInPC','The glassworker holds finished decor because the players PC has no room.','''soft_smile~Our new decoration has arrived before its empty space. We can rearrange.|Capacity needs adjusting before the finished decoration can be stored.|Make room for it. They will keep it safe.|I like that there is no rush to take it away.|A place for the finished piece should come before the move.|The masterpiece has been completed; its accommodation is still under negotiation.|Even the furniture has encountered our impressive talent for full storage.|We should clear a proper slot before transferring the new piece.|A beautiful thing can wait for a place that welcomes it.|Time to edit the collection so the new piece can actually fit.|I would like to plan where it belongs before collecting it.''')
add('institute_strong_child','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_WowYoureStrong','A child admires the players strength and wishes to become a trainer.','''soft_smile~A future trainer just got a very exciting reason to start dreaming.|A striking experience can inspire a lasting interest.|Start by caring for a partner. Strength comes with work.|That kind of admiration feels like something to be careful with.|A kind trainer is a good person for a child to look up to.|An adventure has acquired one very hopeful new admirer.|We have apparently become somebody's example. Mildly alarming, rather sweet.|I hope their curiosity carries them into lots of good practice.|May the dream include the gentle parts of having a partner.|That admiration deserves a gracious answer.|I would ask what Pokemon they would like to meet first.''')
add('institute_sleeping_child','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_EveryoneWentUpstairs','A child woke to discover everyone had gone upstairs.','''surprised~A nap with an unexpectedly empty ending. We should help them find everyone.|They missed the movement while asleep. A simple explanation may reassure them.|Stay close. We will make sure they are all right.|That would feel lonely to wake up to.|I would help them find a familiar adult.|The nap concluded with an entirely different arrangement of people.|Everyone vanished upstairs. An ambitious trick to play on a sleeper.|A quick check upstairs should answer where everyone went.|Waking to an empty room can make a place feel strange.|A familiar face would make this sudden change less confusing.|I would want to know whether someone checked on the child.''')
add('institute_weather_cases','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_NoticingAbnormalWeather','A researcher reports temporary isolated droughts and heavy rain across Hoenn.','''surprised~Dry here, soaking there. Those little patches sound worth watching carefully.|Isolated, temporary events still deserve careful records and comparison.|Good that someone is tracking it. Weather affects people fast.|That sounds unsettling, even when it only lasts a little while.|People planning their day need to know when the weather changes.|The ordinary forecast has developed a series of rather pointed exceptions.|The sky has apparently declined to behave consistently.|I would compare the reports and check where the instruments were placed.|Small changes in the sky can weigh heavily on lives below.|A very uneven forecast for people trying to make ordinary plans.|I would ask whether the reports come from the same places each time.''')
add('rain_professor','Route119_WeatherInstitute_1F_Text_ProfStudyingRain','A researcher says a rain-loving professor studies practical uses because constant rain harms people.','''soft_smile~The professor likes rain and still remembers the people getting soaked. Good.|A preference tempered by concern for consequences. Sound motivation for research.|Liking rain does not mean ignoring floodwater. Sensible.|I like that they can love it and still see the trouble.|Enough rain helps things grow. Too much can ruin a whole season.|A devotee of rain has wisely declined to romanticize everyone's wet socks.|An enthusiast who has considered the neighbors. Remarkably refreshing.|Finding a useful way to handle excess rain sounds worthwhile.|Love for a thing can include care for what it changes.|A thoughtful distinction between enjoying rain and wearing it all week.|I would be interested in what practical uses they have tried.''')
add('berry_master_shop','Route123_BerryMastersHouse_Text_VisitPrettyPetalFlowerShop','The Berry Master recommends Pretty Petal flower shop and wishes flowers across the world.','''soft_smile~A flower-filled world sounds nice. We should leave room for walking, though.|A lovely recommendation, and a pleasantly ambitious botanical goal.|We can stop by. Good to support people who grow things.|That is a gentle thing to wish for the world.|Flowers on the table can make an ordinary meal feel welcoming.|A local shop recommendation has blossomed into a global plan.|The world has been assigned an extensive floral makeover.|I would like to see what they are growing there.|A few planted seeds can carry a very large hope.|A charming destination for a little color and inspiration.|I wonder which flower they would choose for every town.''')
add('berry_master_daily','Route123_BerryMastersHouse_Text_DoneForToday','The Berry Master ends todays berry gifts and invites another visit.','''soft_smile~Even berry generosity needs a bedtime. We can come back another day.|A daily limit is reasonable. The invitation remains generous.|Enough for today. Thank him and let him rest.|It is kind that there is already another welcome waiting.|There is time to enjoy what we have before collecting more.|The day's botanical hospitality has formally drawn to a close.|The berries have finished their public appearances for today.|A sensible schedule keeps a generous project manageable.|Good things can return without needing to last all day.|A gracious end to today's giving. We can leave it there.|I would enjoy coming back to hear how the garden has changed.''')
add('berry_grandchildren','Route123_BerryMastersHouse_Text_JoyNeverGoesOutOfMyLife','The Berry Masters wife proudly hopes their four grandchildren will surpass her husband.','''soft_smile~Four growing grandchildren and a proud grandparent. That is a full garden of joy.|Her confidence in the next generation is rather lovely.|She is proud of them. Good reason to be happy.|The warmth in that makes the whole house feel different.|A family with plenty of young people to share its knowledge.|The family legacy has four eager possibilities and one delighted witness.|Her husband has acquired four very small future rivals.|Passing knowledge along can build something bigger than one person's work.|Joy has found several familiar faces to keep returning in.|She has a very charming way of boasting about the whole family.|I would ask what each grandchild is most excited to learn.''')
